Fillets: a rounding of a short edge whose contact meets the edge of its
face past the vertex farther than the spine's extension reaches is walked
again over a longer extension, so that the corner cuts it with the face at
the end (mitcad#1256).

The case: the reported part of GitHub mitcad/Mitcad#130, imported from
STEP (every face a B-spline surface, so the blend is walked). A thin wall
(a plane) meets an overhanging end band (a plane leaning 29 degrees) along
a slanted edge of 0.84, whose top vertex lies on an earlier rounding of
radius 2 (between the part's slope and its vertical end wall) that cuts
both: three convex edges, an AllSame end. The edge rounded with 0.75 or 1:
past the top vertex the contact on the wall meets the rounding's edge
0.16 on, but the contact on the band meets it only 0.49 on at 0.75 and
0.63 at 1 (that edge leaves the vertex at 55 degrees to the spine and
curves), and ExtentOneCorner prolongs the
spine by half the edge's length (0.42) whatever the radius. The walk
stopped at the extension's end with that contact still inside the band,
FindFace found no face holding both points, and PerformIntersectionAtEnd
built a corner face folded back on itself, 0.035 out of the body at 0.75
(accepted by the checker) and a self-intersecting wire at 1. At the bottom
vertex at 1 the contact on the wall stopped short of the floor in the same
way. The same edge after the part's floor was rounded with 1 (a sliver of
0.25 left) gave spikes reaching 0.16 and 0.77 out of the body at 1.

ChFi3d_Builder::PerformSetOfSurf: after a rounding's walk, an end at an
AllSame or OnDiff vertex whose last piece reaches the end of the spine's
extension with a contact still inside its face (the other on an edge of the
vertex, or both inside, ChFi3d_EndStoppedShort) is walked again with that
end's extension longer by twice the largest radius; the walk still stops
where both contacts have left their faces. The new walk is kept where both
contacts of each such end then lie on edges; otherwise (a face at the end
that pokes through the blend, which other ends join over) the first walk
is made again, as before. The corner then cuts the blend with the face at
the end between the two points, as for any end whose contacts reach that
face's edges within the extension. Every other fillet is as before.

On the reported part: the corner and its mirror at the wall's other end
build with one blend face, valid, at 0.5, 0.75, 0.9 and 1, removing 0.053,
0.133, 0.202 and 0.256 mm3 (0.75 and 1 before: the folded face, and an
invalid shape); after the floor's rounding the sliver builds at 0.5 to 1,
valid, no made face out of the body by more than 0.003. Synthetic: the same
corner made of planes and a rounding cylinder, its faces converted to
B-splines, rounded with 0.75 and 1: one blend face, valid, the volume
removed within 1e-5 mm3 of the analytic cylinder's that OCCT builds for the
same body with its planes (before: a folded corner face 0.32 out of the
body, and at 1 both ends folded and an invalid shape).

Upstream: new.

